From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:56:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dynarmic: include <vector> in ir_emitter.h for newer libc++

The Windows build (MSYS2 clang64, newest packages on every run) stopped in
dynarmic's precompiled header: "no template named 'vector' in namespace
'std'" in ir/ir_emitter.h. The header uses std::vector without including
<vector>; older libc++ versions pulled it in through other headers, the
newer one doesn't. Android (pinned NDK 27) is not affected.

dynarmic is a submodule, so this patch changes a file inside it: the
workflows apply patches with git apply, which reaches it (git am can't).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
---
 externals/dynarmic/src/dynarmic/ir/ir_emitter.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/externals/dynarmic/src/dynarmic/ir/ir_emitter.h b/externals/dynarmic/src/dynarmic/ir/ir_emitter.h
--- a/externals/dynarmic/src/dynarmic/ir/ir_emitter.h
+++ b/externals/dynarmic/src/dynarmic/ir/ir_emitter.h
@@ -5,6 +5,8 @@
 
 #pragma once
 
+#include <vector>
+
 #include <mcl/stdint.hpp>
 
 #include "dynarmic/ir/acc_type.h"
-- 
2.43.0

